  "description": "MOVING2024 is a multi-modal motor imagery and motor execution dataset pairing 32-channel dry-electrode EEG with Virtual Glove hand-kinematic tracking. Eleven healthy participants performed rest, motor imagery and motor execution triplets for three right-hand movements (open/close, wrist rotation, finger tapping). This version is a MOABB-formatted derivative of the original Zenodo deposit.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded at 500 Hz with a Neuroelectrics Enobio 32 wireless dry-electrode system (10-20 montage, CMS/DRL reference). Each trial had a 2 s fixation followed by a 6 s action period. The rest, motor imagery, motor execution triplet was repeated eight times per subject for each of three right-hand movements, in a cue-based visual paradigm.",
